NavigatorZoneLore={
["Glenumbra"]="Western High Rock is a Breton heartland of feudal estates, ancient ruins and Wyrd traditions. The forests preserve a spiritual relationship with nature that predates the Covenant, while Daggerfall is one of its principal political and commercial centers.",
["Stormhaven"]="Wayrest sits at the center of the Daggerfall Covenant's political ambitions. Its trade routes and noble houses link High Rock to the wider Iliac Bay. Threats to local stability can therefore undermine the entire alliance.",
["Rivenspire"]="The rugged north of High Rock is governed by competing Breton noble houses. Its isolated settlements and Gothic strongholds make the region particularly vulnerable to unrest and supernatural threats.",
["Alik'r Desert"]="The Redguards of Hammerfell carry the martial and maritime traditions of lost Yokuda. Their reverence for the honored dead shapes local attitudes toward necromancy and the burial sites scattered across this desert.",
["Bangkorai"]="This borderland links High Rock and Hammerfell. Breton and Redguard communities share a strategically important passage between kingdoms, making its fortifications and frontier settlements significant to Covenant defense.",
["Stros M'Kai"]="This island off Hammerfell is a crossroads for sailors, merchants and pirates, with Dwemer ruins testifying to an older civilization beneath present-day Redguard society.",
["Betnikh"]="Orc clans inhabit this fortified island, once associated with the Bretons. Its inhabitants' independence and warrior traditions matter to the Covenant's uneasy alliance of peoples.",
["Khenarthi's Roost"]="Named for the Khajiiti deity of winds, this island is a maritime gateway to Elsweyr. Plantations and ports make its security important to the Dominion's trade and diplomacy.",
["Auridon"]="The eastern island of Summerset guards the approaches to the Altmer homeland. Ancient cultural institutions and aristocratic pride shape reactions to the Dominion's alliance with other peoples.",
["Grahtwood"]="Elden Root, built around a colossal graht-oak, serves as the Dominion capital. Bosmeri culture is shaped by the Green Pact with Y'ffre, which makes the forest a sacred living landscape.",
["Greenshade"]="Deep Valenwood preserves Bosmeri traditions and mysterious spiritual powers of the forest. Local authority is often entwined with the land itself, rather than with conventional feudal institutions.",
["Malabal Tor"]="This western Valenwood region is important to the spiritual leadership of the Bosmer. The Silvenar and Green Lady embody complementary aspects of their people's identity.",
["Reaper's March"]="Valenwood meets Elsweyr here, with mixed Bosmer and Khajiit communities. The Khajiiti lunar faith and the authority of the Mane are central to the region's cultural life.",
["Bleakrock Isle"]="This remote Nordic island lies near the coast of Skyrim. Its small fishing communities occupy a vulnerable frontier of the Ebonheart Pact.",
["Bal Foyen"]="Argonian communities and military installations share this coastal gateway into Morrowind, illustrating the practical cooperation required by the Pact's unlikely alliance.",
["Stonefalls"]="Volcanic terrain and ancient Chimer history define this part of Morrowind. Dunmer settlements, ancestral ruins and the Pact's military defenses stand amid a landscape shaped by ash and fire.",
["Deshaan"]="Mournhold is a center of Tribunal worship and Dunmer government. Temple institutions, Great House politics and ordinary farming communities all depend on stability in this fertile region.",
["Shadowfen"]="This swamp of Black Marsh is home to Argonian communities whose lives are entwined with the Hist. Ancient xanmeers and the history of enslavement by outsiders shape the region's tensions.",
["Eastmarch"]="Windhelm is an ancient Nordic seat of power. Clan loyalties, reverence for ancestors and the traditions of the old Nordic kingdoms influence the Pact's northern heartland.",
["The Rift"]="Autumnal forests surround Riften and old Nordic burial sites. Trade, farming and ancient tombs coexist in a region where the history of the Nords remains close to daily life.",
["Coldharbour"]="Molag Bal's realm of Oblivion embodies domination and enslavement. Its distorted landscapes and captive souls make resistance here significant to the freedom of mortals throughout Nirn.",
["Craglorn"]="This rugged border region contains ancient Nedic ruins and mysteries tied to the constellations. Its remote settlements and dangerous ruins invite cooperation among adventurers.",
["Cyrodiil"]="The Imperial heartland is contested by the three alliances during the Interregnum. Control of its keeps and routes is tied to the struggle for the Ruby Throne.",
["Imperial City"]="The capital of the Empire surrounds the White-Gold Tower, a monument inherited from the Ayleids. Daedric occupation and alliance warfare threaten the symbolic center of imperial rule.",
["Wrothgar"]="The mountains of northern High Rock are central to Orcish identity and the rebuilding of Orsinium. Competing religious traditions honoring Malacath and Trinimac influence its clans and politics.",
["Hew's Bane"]="Abah's Landing is a wealthy port on a harsh peninsula of Hammerfell. Merchant power, corruption and the criminal underworld offer competing paths to influence.",
["Gold Coast"]="Anvil and Kvatch preserve the civic traditions of western Cyrodiil amid the fractured Empire. Trade and political intrigue coexist with the secretive cult of Sithis.",
["Vvardenfell"]="Red Mountain dominates this sacred Dunmer island. The Tribunal temple, Great Houses and Ashlander tribes hold differing views of history, faith and authority.",
["Clockwork City"]="Sotha Sil's hidden mechanical realm reflects an attempt to understand and reshape creation. Its inhabitants live amid artificial landscapes and devices of extraordinary sophistication.",
["Summerset"]="The Altmer homeland preserves ancient magical and social institutions. Opening its borders challenges entrenched traditions and brings outsiders into contact with its guarded heritage.",
["Murkmire"]="Southern Black Marsh preserves Argonian traditions shaped by the Hist and the cycle of change. Ancient stone ruins contrast with living communities adapted to the wetlands.",
["Blackwood"]="Imperial and Argonian communities meet along the border of Cyrodiil and Black Marsh. Leyawiin is a commercial gateway, while the surrounding wetlands preserve a distinct cultural landscape.",
["Deadlands"]="Mehrunes Dagon's realm embodies destruction, change and revolution. Its hostile terrain reflects the power of its Daedric ruler.",
["Fargrave"]="This independent crossroads of Oblivion hosts mortals and Daedra in a trading society that does not belong to a single Daedric Prince.",
["High Isle"]="The Systres archipelago is a maritime center of Breton noble culture, chivalric orders and diplomacy, alongside older druidic traditions.",
["Galen"]="The island preserves living druidic traditions rooted in Y'ffre and the natural world. The various druid circles differ in their interpretations of their heritage.",
["Telvanni Peninsula"]="House Telvanni's magically independent culture shapes this eastern region of Morrowind, while Necrom is a sacred city associated with the Dunmer dead.",
["Apocrypha"]="Hermaeus Mora's realm gathers forbidden and forgotten knowledge. Its libraries and strange inhabitants reflect the dangerous pursuit of secrets.",
["West Weald"]="Skingrad and the surrounding Colovian countryside preserve Imperial agricultural and civic traditions near the border of Valenwood.",
["Solstice"]="This island is a meeting place of distinct cultures and a strategic setting for the struggle against the Worm Cult.",
["Northern Elsweyr"]="Anequina is a Khajiiti homeland of dry grasslands, ancient kingdoms and lunar spirituality. Rimmen is an important political and commercial center.",
["Southern Elsweyr"]="Pellitine's coastal settlements and tropical landscapes are linked by maritime trade and Khajiiti traditions. Ancient Dragonguard history also connects the region to dragon hunting.",
["Western Skyrim"]="Solitude is a major Nordic political and maritime center. The mountains and subterranean Blackreach preserve traces of ancient Nordic and Dwemer history.",
["The Reach"]="The Reachfolk maintain distinct clan traditions and spiritual practices in this mountainous borderland, long contested by neighboring kingdoms.",
["The Night Market"]="A dangerous gathering place in Fargrave where rival factions compete for influence and rewards. Its activities depend on the active event cycle."
}
